bug 8.
.SH BUGS
.B It has never failed,
on either the compiled or the interpreted path, before or after the
reference counts were made atomic.
The race it is built for is real by construction \(em the emitted code
was a plain read-modify-write on a field several threads touch \(em but
this does not demonstrate it, and so it cannot demonstrate a fix either.
Treat a failure here as significant and a pass as weak evidence.
.PP
It cannot see reference counts, only their consequences, and only when
the freed block is reused in a way that changes a field it checks.
